REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 5  1. Executive Summary  This General Report consolidates the full proceedings of the March 2026 Ordinary Session of the North West Regional Assembly (NWRA)   —   the statutory 2025 Accounts Session and first ordinary session of the second mandate   —   held at the Assembly Auditorium in Bamenda from Monday 25 May to Friday 29 May 2026. It merges the official minutes of Day 1, the comprehensive minutes of Day 2, the Day 3 session report, and the minutes of the Closing Sitting into a single audit-ready working document. All resolutions, deliberations and recommendations are flagged throughout the text and re-stated in consolidated registers in Sections 8 to 10.  The session was convened by the President of the Regional Executive Council (REC), Prof. Fru Fobuzshi ANGWAFO III, pursuant to Decision No. 00096630 of 14 May 2026, and was originally scheduled for March 2026 before postponement occasioned by the March parliamentary Congress and the April 2026 pontifical visit to the Region. It opened under the theme of accountability, transparency and regional development.  Headline Outcomes  •   Committee   leadership   completed:   chairpersons,   vice-chairpersons   and secretaries were elected for all seven committees (five in the House of Divisional   Representatives,   two   in   the   House   of   Chiefs),   curing   the representation gap left after December 2025 and restoring compliance with Sections 353 – 356 of Law No. 2019-024.  •   2025 Accounts adopted:   the Administrative Account, Management Account, Finance Control Report and Stores Account for the 2025 financial year were

--- Page 6 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 6  examined,   debated   and   adopted,   with   an   overall   budget   execution   rate confirmed at 97.5%.  •   2026 Budget adjusted upward:   the adjusted 2026 budget was voted at 20,808,152,316 FCFA (read at Day 3)   —   a figure read as 20,818,152,360 FCFA at the Closing Sitting; the discrepancy is flagged for reconciliation. The  trajectory rose from 3 billion at the Assembly’s creation to roughly   20 billion FCFA.  •   Eight deliberations passed:   covering the four 2025 accounts, the 2026 adjusted budget, staff-recruitment authorisation, hall-leasing revenue, and the creation of an Anti-Corruption Unit   —   all transmitted to the House of Chiefs within the 24-hour window required by Section 345(1) and approved.  •   Governance and welfare innovations:   a CONAC-compliant Anti-Corruption Unit was created; a psychosocial- support keynote reframed members’ mental  health as a governance issue; and a 2026 Zenith group health-insurance framework and the CIMA regulatory code were presented.  •   Capacity building:   expert sessions covered the General Code of Regional and Local Authorities and the Special Status, the Environmental and Social Impact Assessment (ESIA) of the Bamenda – Bafut – Wom road, and Disaster Risk Management.  RECURRENT CONCERN   –   PUNCTUALITY   Each sitting commenced between one-and-a-half and two hours behind schedule. The chair repeatedly raised the financial and reputational cost of chronic lateness and called for a deliberate culture change.

--- Page 7 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 7  KEY FISCAL CONCERN   –   ZERO LOCAL TAX   The entire 2025 year-end deficit (approximately 225 million FCFA carried to 2026) is attributable to the failure of a 600 million FCFA local-tax revenue projection to materialise. Not a single franc was collected against that line.  2. Session Identification and Legal Basis  2.1 Formal Particulars  Field   Particulars  Document Type   Consolidated General Report (Official Minutes of Session)  Session   March 2026 Ordinary Session   —   2025 Accounts Session (statutory)  Mandate   First ordinary session of the Second Mandate  Dates   Monday 25 May 2026 to Friday 29 May 2026  Venue   Auditorium of the North West Regional Assembly, Bamenda  Commencement   9:00 a.m. daily (scheduled)  Theme   Accountability, Transparency and Regional Development   —   2025 Fiscal Accounts  Convening Authority   Prof. Fru Fobuzshi ANGWAFO III, President, Regional Executive Council  Convening Instrument   Decision No. 00096630 of 14 May 2026 (modifying Decision No. 0009699663 of 8 May 2026)

--- Page 8 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 8  Field   Particulars  Prepared by   Documentation Production Cell   —   NWRA  Classification   Official Working Document   —   For Institutional Use  2.2 Legal and Regulatory Basis  The session was convened and conducted pursuant to the following instruments:  •   The Constitution of the Republic of Cameroon (notably Article 62 on the Special Status of the North West and South West Regions).  •   Law No. 2019-024 of 24 December 2019 instituting the General Code of Regional and Local Authorities (notably Sections 208, 278, 327, 345, 353 – 356, 379, 406, 467 – 471 and 476).  •   Law No. 2024-020 of 23 December 2024 on public finance.  •   Law No. 2018-011 of 11 July 2018 on the code of transparency and good governance in the management of public finance.  •   Decree No. 2012/109 of 14 March 2012 appointing the Governor of the North West Region.  •   Order No. 0018177 of 31 December 2025 on the implementation, monitoring and control of budget execution for the 2026 financial year.  •   Order No. 2026-001876L/MINFI/MINDEVEL of 31 December 2025 on support for accounting operations of regional and local authorities.  •   Order No. 00150 of 24 December 2025 on the election of the President and members of the Regional Executive Council.  •   Presidential Decree No. 2006/088 of 13 March 2006 creating the National Anti- Corruption Commission (CONAC).

--- Page 9 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 9  •   Law No. 86/016 of 6 December 1986 on civil protection and disaster risk management.  3. Attendance and Quorum  The North West Regional Assembly is composed of ninety (90) members   —   seventy (70) Divisional Representatives (House of Divisional Representatives, HDR) and twenty (20) members drawn from the traditional command (House of Chiefs, HOC)  —   reflecting the sociological diversity of the Region. Honourable Members of Parliament and Mayors attend in a consultative, non-deliberative capacity.  At the formal roll call opening Day 1, an initial quorum check recorded seven (7) members at the precise roll-call point; additional members of the House of Chiefs and invited dignitaries were already present. The President of the REC declared the session valid and proceedings commenced, with members joining through the morning.   A   full   roll   call   subsequently   recorded   sixty-six   (66)   Divisional Representatives present by mid-session. Quorum was confirmed and constituted on Day 2; on Day 3 it was largely attained and a formal roll call was dispensed with.  3.1 Distinguished Dignitaries in Attendance  Across the sitting days the Assembly welcomed: His Excellency the Governor of the North   West   Region   (Representative   of   the   State);   the   Public   Independent Conciliator; the Procurator and members of the Judiciary; the SDO for Mezam and the City Mayor of Bamenda; the Commanders of the Joint Military Region and the 5th Gendarmerie Region; the Vice-Chancellor of the University of Bamenda; Honourable Members of Parliament; Mayors of the Region; Regional Delegates and Chiefs of Services; the members of the House of Chiefs; and traditional, religious, civil-society, political-party and media representatives, alongside development partners and special guests.

--- Page 10 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 10  4. Day 1   —   Monday, 25 May 2026  Day 1 was devoted to the ceremonial opening, the completion of committee leadership   elections,   the   adoption   of   the   December   2025   minutes,   and   the  Governor’s special report on the state of the Region. The President of the REC, Prof.  Fru Fobuzshi ANGWAFO III, presided.  4.1 Opening Ceremonials and Convening Decision  The Assembly rose for the National Anthem, after which a Muslim prayer (Honourable Adamo Ali Sule) and a Christian prayer (Reverend Dr. Anya Mott) invoked divine guidance, unity and peace upon the proceedings   —   reflecting the  Region’s multi -faith character. The Secretary-General then read, in full, Decision No. 00096630 of 14 May 2026 convening the 2026 Accounts Session, which fixed the dates (25 – 29 May 2026), the daily 9:00 a.m. start, and an agenda spanning committee elections, examination of the 2025 administrative, management and  stores   accounts,   the   Finance   Controller’s   and   Stores   Accountant’s   reports,  deliberation and adoption of the State account, the 2026 budget adjustment, and interactive presentations on the Code, insurance, psychosocial support, and the Bamenda – Wom road ESIA.  4.2   Opening Address by the President of the Regional Executive Council  The President explained that the session, originally scheduled for March 2026, had been delayed by the March parliamentary Congress and the April 2026 pontifical visit of Pope Francis to the Region   —   which he characterised as a universal, non- political moral appeal for peace whose momentum leaders had a duty to sustain. He cited the rehabilitation of Bamenda Airport and the improvement of urban access roads as tangible symbols of regional progress.

--- Page 11 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 11  Drawing on the “three R’s,” the President offered a governance philosophy:  subtraction and division stand for conflict and underdevelopment, while addition and multiplication stand for collaboration, peace and growth   —   and he urged members  to “add and multiply” the dividends of peace. He framed the session as a landmark  first statutory accounts session of the second mandate, embodying continuity, renewal, reconciliation, reform and the restoration of Ubuntu heritage values.  Critically, the President drew urgent attention to an institutional gap: during the December 2025 Session as of Right, committees had been chosen without observing the legal requirement for equitable representation, leaving four divisions   —   Boyo, Donga-Mantung,   Menchum   and   Momo   —   effectively   unrepresented   across committees, and with chairpersons and secretaries not yet elected, in breach of Sections 353 – 356 of Law No. 2019-024. He directed that completing the committee elections be the first substantive business of the session, ahead of any financial deliberations.  RESOLUTION D1-A   The completion of committee leadership elections (chairpersons, vice-chairpersons, secretaries) was made the first order of business so as to cure the December 2025 representation gap and restore compliance with Sections 353 – 356 of Law No. 2019-024.  LOGISTICAL INNOVATION   –   MEAL TICKET SYSTEM   A colour-coded, date-specific and non-transferable meal-coupon system was introduced (Day 1 coupon: white) to ensure equitable food distribution and address prior complaints of supplies running out before all members were served.

--- Page 12 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 12  4.3 Election of Committee Executives  An independent Electoral Commission was established to ensure impartiality, chaired by Mr. Taman John (Regional Delegate, MINDEVEL), with the Secretary- General and four other members. The governing criteria were: no two leaders on a list from the same division; at least one female member per list; no division leading more than one of the seven committees; regard to professional competence; and a three-position list system (Chairperson, Vice-Chairperson, Secretary), with a 30- minute submission window and 1 – 3 minutes of presentation per list.  After deliberation, voting and validation, the following executives were elected:  Committee   House   Chairperson   Vice-Chair   Secretary  Admin. & Legal Affairs / Standing Orders  HDR   Sonju George (Bui)  Hon. Mba Sattu (Momo)  Hon. Benyala Gondwintapong  Education   HDR   Sondjo George (Bui)   —   —  Health, Population, Social & Cultural Affairs, Youth & Sports  HDR   Mme Trida Bongsin-Mwan  Son Grace Sa (Boyo)   —  Finance, Infrastructure, Planning & Economic Dev.  HDR   Hon. Ojambé Stephen (Momo)  Hon. Gordon Agnelin (Mezam)  Hon. Sadatou Sallie (Momo)

--- Page 13 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 13  Committee   House   Chairperson   Vice-Chair   Secretary  Environment, Regional Dev., State Property, Town Planning & Housing  HDR   Mme Matilda Bengu (Boyo)  Njo Oliver Anno (Momo)  Omdonga (Maton)  Admin., Legal, Education, Health, Social & Cultural, Youth & Sports  HOC   HRM Ganeshios Ndiyuan Gufo  HRM Nguyen Ns Melensh- Shan  HRM Quanga Pita (Boyo)  Finance, Infrastructure, Economic Dev., Environment, Housing  HOC   HRM Fonju Wilson III  HRM Nguyen Bangansi III (Momo)  HRM Kunde Powanto Timoti  HDR = House of Divisional Representatives; HOC = House of Chiefs; HRM = His Royal Majesty.  The Finance Committee was the most competitive, attracting three lists; Honourable Ojambé Stephen was elected Chairperson. The Health Committee returned a female chairperson (Mme Trida Bongsin- Mwan), and the Environment Committee’s single  list (Mme Matilda Bengu, Boyo) was approved unanimously with 12 votes. An observation on placement without regard to professional competence was addressed by the Secretary-General, who noted that all fourteen committee members serve and contribute collaboratively and that geographic and gender representation takes precedence in composition. A concern on the standing of youth members was

--- Page 14 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 14  acknowledged without amendment, the President noting that age should be no impediment to meaningful contribution.  4.4 Adoption of the December 2025 Minutes  The minutes of the December 2025 Ordinary Session (8 – 11 December 2025) were read,   covering   the   joint   opening;   the   School   Map   and   Third   Health   Map presentations; the 2025 Project Execution Report; committee and divisional reports across all seven divisions;   the House of Chiefs’ examination of the 2026 budget; and  the adoption by acclamation of the 2026 Budget at 14.6 billion FCFA following transfers from the Central Government.  The minutes of the Session as of Right (16 December 2025), dedicated to electing the Regional Executive Council, were also read: convened by the Governor under Section 208(2); 90 of 90 councillors present; a single list led by Prof. Fru Fobuzshi ANGWAFO III elected with 88 valid ballots of 90 (97.7% in favour). Both sets of December 2025 minutes were formally adopted without objection.  RESOLUTION D1-B   The minutes of the December 2025 Ordinary Session (8 – 11 December 2025) and of the December 2025 Session as of Right (16 December 2025) were formally adopted by the Assembly.  4.5 Governor’s Special Report on the State of the Region (2025)  His Excellency the Governor delivered a comprehensive report on state-service activity for 2025. Salient points, by sector, are summarised below.  Governance, Security and Local Administration  •   Sustained supervision of decentralised services; the security situation, though still constrained, improved markedly on the prior year, with progressive pacification of formerly disturbed areas. The Governor described residual

--- Page 15 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 15  militancy as the “last kick of a dying horse” and urged enrolment of ex - combatants in the DDR programme.  •   Many councils remain delocalised in Bamenda but are increasingly functional. Council project-execution rates varied sharply   —   Kambo Council reached 100% of CCCR projects while JAKIRI Council attained only 39.8%. The Governor flagged salaries paid without commensurate output and called for performance-based accountability, and for all council boards to join the electronic award and public-contracts platform.  Economy, Infrastructure and Budget Execution  •   The 2025 global budget allocation for the Region stood at 94,418,984,000 FCFA. Of 6.7 billion FCFA in public-investment projects, 4.24 billion had been executed by February 2026; physical execution reached 138.8% against a financial execution rate of 90.0%.  •   Road works advanced on the Bamenda – Wom road, the Parana Wings road  (≈90– 94%), and Namu rehabilitation; the Prime Minister commissioned the Bamenda urban road. Energy instability caused widespread blackouts; water projects funded at 959 million FCFA progressed at 18.2% – 36.76% execution.  Agriculture, Education, Health and Youth  •   Agriculture: 471 tonnes of seed distributed; ≈188,000 cattle and other livestock  vaccinated; 65 fish species produced by 489 farmers across 1,097 ponds; bean  prices rose ≈30% on erratic rainfall; CIFT supported some 2,100 farmers across  poultry, livestock, fish, bee and milk production.  •   Education: secondary enrolment rose to 107,700 (2025 – 26) from 83,846; primary enrolment of 219,573 across 1,907 schools; improved examination  performance.   Higher   education:   ≈28,000   students   at   the   University   of  Bamenda, coordinating 39 private institutions.

--- Page 16 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 16  •   Health: no malaria cases recorded in the review period; vaccination campaigns  reaching ≈90% of target children under five; Maternal and Child Health and  Nutrition Action Weeks delivered; expired medicines collected and destroyed. Youth: a guidance-training programme for 2,121 volunteers launched, and a woman-led STEM competition surfaced young female innovators.  The Governor concluded that the overall situation was globally satisfactory despite persistent challenges, and appealed for sustained collaboration to consolidate peace and relaunch the economy. A special address by Miss Solita Dasi, First Runner-Up of Miss North West, followed, advocating youth empowerment, obedience, wisdom and humility in leadership.  4.6 Day 1 Resolutions and Decisions  No.   Decision / Resolution   Authority  D1   Session declared valid and proceedings opened, notwithstanding the initial low roll-call quorum.   P/REC  D2   Electoral Commission established to conduct committee- executive elections.  P/REC & REC  D3   Seven committee executive teams (HDR × 5, HOC × 2) duly elected and validated.  Electoral Commission / Assembly  D4   Minutes of the December 2025 Ordinary Session adopted.   Regional Assembly  D5   Minutes of the December 2025 Session as of Right adopted.   Regional Assembly

--- Page 17 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 17  No.   Decision / Resolution   Authority  D6   Colour-coded meal-ticket system approved and implemented from Day 1.   P/REC  D7   REC Performance Report and formal account presentations deferred to Day 2.   P/REC  D8   Photo session held documenting the newly elected committee executives with the Representative of State.  President, RA  5. Day 2   —   Tuesday, 26 May 2026  Day 2 was the financial heart of the session: the 2025 Performance Report, the election of a Pro-Term Chairperson, and the presentation, debate and formal adoption of the 2025 Administrative, Management and Stores Accounts, followed by the 2026 Zenith group health-insurance presentation and a regulatory lecture on the CIMA Code. The sitting began about 1 hour 30 minutes behind schedule; the President again pressed the cost of tardiness and asked that regional development documentaries be screened during delays.  5.1 2025 Performance Report  Presented by the President of the REC under Section 467 of Law No. 2019/024, structured across four statutory programmes (activities paid up to 31 January 2026 included per law):  •   Programme 1   –   Basic Social Services:   theatre and surgical units, emergency and   outpatient   departments,   mother-and-child   blocks,   solar   backup   and equipment across numerous district and regional hospitals; classroom and laboratory blocks, examination-fee support for over 700 needy students, science

--- Page 18 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 18  kits and computers, and a cooperation agreement with Promethea (London) for 135 intelligent classrooms.  •   Programme 2   –   Economic Development and Environment:   advanced construction   of   the   Mutan   Market;   the   Digital   Entrepreneurship   Hub; establishment of the North West Development and Investment Fund; Phase 1 completed and Phase 2 commenced on the Regional Administrative Building and Regional Lodge; rehabilitation of Regional Road No. 512; and tree planting and catchment protection.  •   Programme 3   –   Citizenship, Culture, Sports and Youth:   reforestation protecting sacred sites; capacity-building for over 40 traditional rulers; more than 60 interns hosted; and the auditorium provided pro bono to over 35 civil- society organisations for more than 60 days.  •   Programme 4   –   Governance and Local Administration:   health and vehicle insurance; fleet maintenance and service vehicles; mission allowances; capacity seminars; five sessions financed; and commencement of the Administrative Manual of Procedures.  KEY CHALLENGE   –   PEACE & DEVELOPMENT INITIATIVE (PDI)  The President disclosed that some PDI workers were unpaid because unauthorised intermediaries collected funds without distributing them to beneficiaries. This governance failure was acknowledged as requiring urgent correction, with members urged to ensure funds reach workers directly.  5.2 Election of the Pro-Term Chairperson  Pursuant to Section 469(1) of the Code, a Pro-Term Chairperson was required to preside over examination and adoption of the Administrative Account, to remove the conflict of interest inherent in the President (as Authorising Officer) presiding

--- Page 19 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 19  over his own account. The REC participated in deliberations but withdrew during voting. Honourable Malou declined nomination, having twice ceded leadership opportunities to younger members and Muslim colleagues.  Candidate   Remarks   Votes  Hon. Kibu Mohendri Tumi  Original nominee   —  DECLARED ELECTED  27  Hon. Fonjinda   Nominated by Chief T.B. Stanley   24  Hon. Matida Benigo  Nominated following  Hon. Malou’s  withdrawal  10  RESOLUTION D2-A   Honourable Kibu Mohendri Tumi was declared elected Pro-Term Chairperson with 27 votes (of 61 effective ballots cast), to preside over the examination and adoption of the 2025 Administrative Account.  5.3 2025 Administrative Account  Presented by the President as Authorising Officer and Vote Holder. The budget was initially adopted by Deliberation No. 2024/0632 of 30 December 2024 and adjusted by Deliberation No. 2025/156 of 23 April 2025.  Budget Item   CFA Francs  Initial Approved Budget (Dec 2024)   5,625,878,285  Adjusted Budget (Apr 2025)   10,331,257,601  Total Revenue Committed and Validated   10,073,186,323

--- Page 20 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 20  Budget Item   CFA Francs  Overall Execution Rate   96.6%  Operating / Recurrent Commitments   1,570,025,654 (90.50%)  Investment Commitments   8,503,857,869 (98.92%)  Net Deficit Carried Forward to 2026   (225,495,159)  Revenue performance by source was uneven: the MINDEVEL subvention of 1 billion FCFA was received in full (100%); tender-file proceeds (137.4%), plow-back of unclaimed allowances (175.8%) and the accounting carry-forward (466.9%) over- performed; while the projected 600 million FCFA in local-tax revenue realised nothing (0%)   —   the sole cause of the deficit. The President defended ambitious projection as legally sound: unbudgeted revenue cannot be spent, so it is better to project high and adjust mid-year than to under-budget and be unable to deploy funds received.  Payment prioritisation in 2025 was: (1) all five sessions of the deliberating organ fully funded; (2) all staff salaries paid for the full 12 months; (3) all REC allowances paid for 12 months; with third- party suppliers (≈225 million FCFA) deferred to  2026. A SWOT analysis confirmed high execution (97.51% in 2025 vs 97.46% in 2024) and investment allocation well above the 60% statutory minimum (the Assembly at 83%), while flagging dependency on external resources (PROLOC, PPRD, FAICOM) for roughly 49% of income.  5.4 Report of the Financial Controller  Presented pursuant to Decree No. 77-41 of 3 February 1977 and Law No. 2018/012 of 11 July 2018. The Controller confirmed overall budget execution at 97.5% (investment 98.6%; recurrent 92.0%) and identified five key challenges: (1) limited financial autonomy, with 49% of income lodged within partner institutions and 36%

--- Page 21 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 21  routed via the Paymaster General; (2) the complexity of the multi-stakeholder PDI; (3) digital limitations   —   the SIMBA and PROGBIS systems are physically separated, require manual file transfers, and run only in French; (4) zero local-tax collection; and (5) sixty late investment files outstanding at the 30 November statutory closure, compounded by understaffing.  RECOMMENDATIONS   –   FINANCIAL CONTROLLER   Finalise and adopt the   procedural   manual   (including   the   PDI);   run   public-finance   training workshops; develop an annual tentative commitment plan; strengthen monitoring of multi-year programmes; urgently trigger local-tax disbursement; equip and add staff to the Finance Control unit; and provide English-language versions of SIMBA / PROGBIS for the Anglophone Region.  5.5 2025 Management Account  Presented   by   the   Regional   Treasurer,   the   Treasurer’s   counterpart   to   the  Administrative Account, destined for the State Audit Court (Chambre des Comptes). Global   internal   revenue   collected   at   the   Regional   Treasury   in   2025   was 1,042,078,748 FCFA (MINDEVEL 1 billion in two instalments; tender-file sales 13,741,611; plow-back 17,582,137; carry-forward 302,352,411).  Trial Balance / Result (Class 5)   CFA Francs  Total Functional Revenue Collected   1,344,481,159  Total Functional Expenditure Paid   1,343,622,447  Budgetary Result (cash balance, 31 Dec 2025)   +808,712  Total Operational Commitments (Vote Holder)   1,568,283,404  Accounting Result / Unpaid Bills to 2026   (223,852,245)

