REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 22  Trial Balance / Result (Class 5)   CFA Francs  Fund Movements   –   PMG to Regional Treasury   772,196,516  Total Taxes Declared and Paid   109,236,243  The Treasurer noted minor anomalies arising from the upgraded CIMBA application (a   collective   issue   across   all   regional   assemblies),   to   be   corrected   before transmission to the State Audit Court, and renewed appeals for additional computers, capacity training and staffing.  5.6 2025 Stores Account  Presented by the Stores Accountant, covering procurement, distribution and stock management. Against an adjusted budget of 10,331,257,601 FCFA (an 83.64% increase on the initial budget), 83% was directed to visible infrastructure and equipment. Key supply values included furniture (192,802,469 FCFA), tools and devices (280,380,203 FCFA), and library / teaching materials (162,186,646 FCFA), with a modest 12,507,285 FCFA carried forward. The consolidated grand total of consumables,   durables   and   services   rendered   stood   at   2,719,195,719   FCFA, supported by a photographic annexe.  5.7 Open Floor   —   Questions and Responses  Substantive contributions and the responses they drew included:  •   Project execution and quality control:   members may not conduct statutory technical follow-up (reserved for qualified engineers) but have every right to social follow-up   —   monitoring timelines and visible progress and raising the alarm on delays, which triggers corrective action by the State engineer.  •   Language barrier:   the French-only CIMBA software (developed by PNDP, supported by PACFI) was the reason the Treasurer lectured rather than read the

