REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 24  RESOLUTION D2-B   –   2025 ACCOUNTS ADOPTED   The 2025 Administrative Account, Management Account and Stores Account of the North West Regional Assembly are duly ADOPTED as presented, with the proviso that the Finance Controller shall issue further clarification on the personnel- payment ambiguities for the record. The adopted accounts are to be transmitted to the District Administration (supervisory authority) and thereafter to the State Audit Court, per Articles 469 and 471.  5.9 Zenith 2026 Health-Insurance Policy and the CIMA Framework  Zenith Insurance (Bamenda Branch) presented the 2026 group policy (1 January – 31 December 2026): Group 1 (Executives) at 100% coverage (2 million FCFA in Cameroon; 5 million abroad) and Group 2 (Councillors and Staff) at 80% (up to 1 million FCFA), covering health, personal accident and funeral expenses, via purchase-order or reimbursement and a biometric card. The 2025 claims deadline was extended to 10 June 2026, and all January – May 2026 bills were confirmed reimbursable on presentation of originals.  Members raised activation delays (a member turned away in January despite premiums paid), disorganised delivery, mid-year-start value-for-money concerns, burdensome multi-unit hospital protocols, card non-recognition by providers, and travel-cover ambiguity. The Presiding Officer directed three corrective measures, captured below.  RESOLUTION D2-C   –   INSURANCE REVIEW   (1) The Administrative and Legal Affairs Committee to be provided the full Zenith contract for clause review; (2) a clause to be negotiated allowing claims to be processed at the Bamenda branch rather than referred to Yaoundé; and (3) a formal questionnaire to be issued to all members auditing claim experiences for data-driven reform.

--- Page 25 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 25  The Regional Chief of Insurance and Monetary Affairs then set out the CIMA Code: the three conditions for a valid contract (written terms with risks, premiums and exclusions per Article 8; premium paid; full CIMA compliance); the claims- declaration procedure (within five working days, with full documentation); the  insurer’s Article 15 obligation to pay valid claims within the policy timeframe; the  two-year limitation (Articles 28 – 29); and the escalation pathway from the insurer to the National Directorate of Insurance and the Regional Commission for the Control of Insurance.  6. Day 3   —   Thursday, 28 May 2026  Day 3 was the working heart of the session: a morning that turned inward to  members’ mental health and a committee orientation, and an afternoon of  committee and divisional reports, the adoption of the 2025 accounts as working documents, and eight deliberations   —   including the creation of an Anti-Corruption Unit. Quorum was largely attained and the roll call dispensed with.  6.1 Psychosocial Keynote   —   “Bury What No One Sees”  Madam Ma Anyangwe, clinical psychologist and traumatologist at the Bamenda  Regional Hospital, reframed members’ wellbeing as a governance issue. She distinguished the visible “camera” (curated images) from the invisible record of  trauma each member carries, noting that members living in an active insecurity zone since 2016 absorb both direct trauma (threats, displacement, hyper-vigilance) and vicarious trauma from graphic images and stories circulating daily on social media.  Unaddressed, individual trauma becomes institutional trauma   —   manifesting as presenteeism, reactive rather than strategic decisions, bills passed without scrutiny, unread reports, eroded trust, and a public that stops believing in the Assembly. She

--- Page 26 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 26  introduced the Adolescent Wellness Center at the Bamenda Regional Hospital (launched 27 January 2024).  RECOMMENDATIONS   –   PSYCHOSOCIAL SUPPORT   Establish a team- based crisis-response protocol; use the on-site health-screening team; build emotional-regulation skills and route members to confidential counselling via the Commissioner for Health; stop sharing graphic images on WhatsApp; aim for 6 –  8 ho urs’ sleep; practise peer support and immediate conflict mediation; and lean  on family and spiritual support.  RESOLUTION D3-A   –   REGION-WIDE DISSEMINATION   The Chair directed the Secretariat to capture the audio-visual presentation and disseminate it region-wide (citing Sections 471 and 476 of the Code), and called for more group therapy   —   “nothing in this house is meant to be kept in a silo.”  6.2 Committee Orientation (Hon. Questa)  With new committees freshly elected, Honourable Questa briefed the five standing committees on their missions under Law No. 2019/024 and the Special Status instrument: Administrative & Legal Affairs (guardian of legality and procedure); Finance, Infrastructure, Planning & Economic Development (a recovery-and- transformation mandate treating finance strategically); Education (safeguarding the Anglo-Saxon tradition and promoting technical, vocational and digital learning); Population, Social & Cultural Affairs, Youth & Sports (public health, welfare, psychosocial recovery); and Environment, Regional Development, State Property, Town Planning & Housing (sustainability, climate resilience and land use). The President urged development that is community-driven through the Participatory Development Approach, crowdfunding for structural development, and a bamboo- centred development plan.

--- Page 27 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 27  6.3 Committee Reports  Education Committee  Reported a 100% execution rate for 2025 education projects.  RECOMMENDATIONS   –   EDUCATION   Revamp agriculture and hands-on subjects within a review of the Anglo-Saxon model; fully support and seek further partners for the intelligent-classrooms initiative; reopen the aborted National Forum on Education; and settle outstanding classroom-construction debts ahead of the new school year.  Administrative, Legal Affairs & Standing Orders Committee  RESOLUTIONS   –   ADMIN & LEGAL AFFAIRS   (1) Congratulate the President of the Regional Assembly and team for the quality of reports; (2) congratulate the Representative of State / Governor for keeping both Houses abreast of the regional situation; and (3) call on the administration to provide, within two weeks, physical copies of key legal texts   —   the Constitution, the 2019 Decentralisation Code and the Standing Orders.  Finance, Infrastructure, Planning & Economic Development Committee  RECOMMENDATIONS   –   FINANCE   Spend CAC (local-tax) funds promptly to avoid year-end lapse; have devolved ministries transmit functional budgets alongside investment budgets; PREC to write formally to the Prime Minister on devolved competencies (only 6 of 72 transferred, 4 funded); convene the Finance Committee at least one day before budget sessions; mature bankable projects with mayors; ensure at least one project per subdivision; circulate documents early in soft copy; and maintain a 40% functional / 60% investment ratio in 2027.

