REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 30  politicised; the SG and PDI technical team are to hasten controls so the eligible are paid immediately.  “We have had pressure to the point of giving the region collective suicide.  So stop being pressured   —   the state has procedures.”   —   President,  recalling the morning’s psychosocial talk  Project-quality flags were raised in Donga-Mantung (contractors at 0% execution  with ≈30% of time elapsed, at Ako and Nwa) and in Momo (the Guzang Palace  and the Batibo District Hospital fence), with the technical team to investigate and relaunch. The President urged members to track utilisation, not merely construction   —   “a maternity built but unused is a waste of resources.”  6.5 Adoption of the 2025 Accounts and the Eight Deliberations  On a motion by Hon. Gunn Felix Mbouri (seconded by Hon. Nanjo Jusufi Nyonga), members confirmed the principal aggregates agreed and no discrepancy was established.  RESOLUTION D3-B   –   ACCOUNTS AS WORKING DOCUMENTS   The Assembly unanimously approved the 2025 administrative, management and financial (finance-control and stores) accounts as working documents, for transmission to the House of Chiefs and the relevant authorities.  The Secretary-General read each deliberation; members validated all eight in form and content, and they were transmitted to the House of Chiefs within the 24-hour window required by Section 345(1):  #   Deliberation   Decision  1   Voting & adopting the 2025 Administrative Account (Arts. 468 – 471)   Adopted

