REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 31  #   Deliberation   Decision  2  Voting & adopting the 2025 Management Account; copies to MINFI, MINDEVEL and the Audit Bench  Adopted  3   Adopting the 2025 Stores Accountant’s Report  (Art. 278)   Adopted  4   Adopting the 2025 Finance Control Service Report (Art. 278)   Adopted  5   Voting & adopting the 2026 Adjusted Budget (balanced)  Adopted   –  20,808,152,316 FCFA  6   Authorising the REC to recruit staff (MINDEVEL letter No. 000475/L of 19 Feb 2026)  Authorised; file to MINDEVEL  7   Authorising collection / management of hall- leasing revenue  Adopted   –   100,000 FCFA/day  8   Creating an Anti-Corruption Unit (CONAC Decree 2006/088)   Adopted  VERIFY   –   2026 BUDGET FIGURE   The adjusted budget was read as 20,808,152,316 FCFA on Day 3 but as 20,818,152,360 FCFA at the Closing Sitting. The two readings differ; confirm the exact figure against the signed deliberation before publication.  The Hall-Leasing Debate  The leasing deliberation was the day’s liveliest. The SG first read 200,000 FCFA per  day; the President pushed back, recalling that the auditorium had hosted over sixty  associations free of charge in 2025, “buying peace” and goodwill. The fee was

