REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 36  that 36 billion FCFA (Government) and ≈13 billion FCFA (AfDB) had reportedly  been allocated, with questions on the compensation timeline; and an objection to birth- control messaging given the Region’s demographic needs. Mr. Agia clarified  that experts only propose, with compensation and resettlement following AfDB rules and resting with the project owner.  7.5 Committee and Divisional Reports (Reaffirmed)  The Secretary read Letter No. 137/SG/DAG of 28 May 2026 from the President of the House of Chiefs confirming the deliberations had been examined and approved. Committee heads reaffirmed their recommendations (Administrative & Legal, Education, Environment,   Finance and Health), and the House of Chiefs’ combined  report added: strengthening collaboration between traditional and administrative authorities; school rehabilitation and vocational training; addressing inadequate rural healthcare; preserving cultural heritage; a revision of Section 337(2) of Law  No. 2019/024; and an upward review of the Fons’ remuneration in line with their  special status. Divisional reports from Mezam, Momo and Ngoketunjia were consolidated with the common-agenda recommendations.  7.6 Final Adoption of the Eight Deliberations  Noting that some signatures had been appended before formal adoption, members re-signed so signatures reflected the adopted texts. The Secretary-General read the eight deliberations point by point; each was validated. Each takes effect from the date of approval by the Representative of State and is to be registered, published and communicated in English and French.

