REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 38  the prior year with projections to exceed 30 billion FCFA annually over the mandate, and urged equitable distribution across the seven divisions and 31  subdivisions and continued security collaboration (“see something, say something”).  In closing, the President of the Regional Assembly apologised to the Governor for any perceived disrespect, stressed mutual respect as a condition for development, and traced the budget trajectory   —   from 3 billion, to 5 billion, to 10 billion, and now a roughly 20 billion FCFA adjusted budget   —   as concrete evidence that decentralisation is real. He called for budgets to be translated into projects benefiting the vulnerable, the internally displaced and the physically challenged, undertook inter-session work on the Standing Orders and a performance manual, and formally declared the first (March) session of the second mandate closed.  8. Consolidated Financial Summary  The table below consolidates the principal 2025 fiscal aggregates examined during the session and the adjusted 2026 budget.  Indicator   Value  2025 Initial Approved Budget   5,625,878,285 FCFA  2025 Adjusted Budget   10,331,257,601 FCFA  2025 Revenue Committed & Validated   10,073,186,323 FCFA  2025 Overall Execution (Administrative Account)   96.6%  2025 Overall Execution (Finance Controller, confirmed)   97.5%

