--- Page 48 ---
REPUBLIC OF CAMEROON   Peace   –   Work   –   Fatherland  NORTH WEST REGIONAL ASSEMBLY  Assemblée Régionale du Nord Ouest · Special Status Region  March 2026 Session · 2025 Accounts   NWRA · Documentation Production Cell   Page 48  13. Conclusion  The   March   2026   Ordinary   Session   discharged   the   Assembly’s   statutory  accountability obligations for the 2025 financial year and opened the institutional work of the second mandate on a sound footing. Committee leadership was completed in compliance with the law; the 2025 accounts were examined, debated and adopted at a confirmed 97.5% execution rate; and the 2026 budget was adjusted upward to roughly 20 billion FCFA, evidencing the deepening of decentralisation. Beyond the figures, the session matured the As sembly’s governance —   creating a CONAC-compliant Anti- Corruption Unit, treating members’ mental health as a  governance concern, and strengthening environmental and disaster-risk safeguards on major infrastructure.  The recurring themes   —   punctuality, equitable distribution of projects across the seven divisions and thirty-one subdivisions, the structural dependence on external and central resources, the zero local-tax collection, and the imperative that funds reach intended beneficiaries directly   —   frame the priorities for the inter-session period and the next sitting. As a working document, this report should be read alongside the signed deliberations and the official register, with the verification points in Section 12 resolved before formal reliance.

